    id: "ar-7978",
    testNumber: 110,
    title: "Test #110: Why Diwali Doesn't Mean Joy For Pets",
    language: "english",
    category: "up_police_co",
    duration: 15,
    wordCount: 585,
    difficulty: "medium",
    date: "2024-10-31",
    text: "The sudden, intense sounds generated by fireworks can trigger profound distress and anxiety in dogs and other animals. Animals may experience elevated heart rates, uncontrollable shaking and fear. The loud noises can potentially damage hearing in animals too, and in some cases, make dogs go blind. Veterinarian Piyush Patel, director, Companion Animals and Engagement Team, Humane Society International India, said it was essential for pet parents to create a calm environment for their animals during noisy festivals like Diwali. On Diwali, many pets experience heightened stress and anxiety due to the loud noises from fireworks. This can lead to fear, disorientation, and even physical distress. The bright lights and chaotic celebrations can overwhelm pets, causing them to seek refuge or escape. Calming your pets during Diwali can make a big difference to their comfort. Dr Abhijit Pawde, head, Centre for Wildlife, Indian Institute of Veterinary Research, Bareilly, said, We have seen some cases in which dogs suffer from optic amaurosis disease, in which the animal loses eyesight due to the noise when crackers are burst close to their ears. Some people with malicious intent light the crackers near the ears of dogs. He added that the constant bursting of crackers creates panic among animals, who blindly try to run away and could end up being crushed by moving vehicles. Few animals become overaggressive and because they are uncomfortable with crackers, they try to attack and bite the fireworks. This can result in fractures or shattering of their jaw. Veterinarians said it was necessary to set up a quiet, cosy space for pets on such occasions, ensuring their bed, blankets and toys were near. They advise keeping pets away from windows and doors to help muffle noise and the use of rugs and carpets to absorb sound. Do not leave pets alone during the peak bursting of crackers and spend time with them, offer them cuddles, and if they show any signs of distress, consult a veterinarian, they prescribed. Delhi govt has imposed a complete ban on all fireworks this year. Ambika Shukla, trustee, People for Animals, has appealed to people to adhere to the pyrotechnics ban. If you have pets at home or you take care of community dogs, patrol your neighbourhood and report to the authorities if the ban is flouted, suggested Shukla. She added that dogs should be fed and taken for a walk before 5pm on Diwali before the cracker bursting begins and to ensure to put a name tag and contact number on the collar in case the animal flees in panic.\n\nIn the operational architecture of Uttar Pradesh Police, technological adaptation has transformed administrative transparency and tactical responsiveness. The integration of modern analytical dashboards enables precinct supervisors to track incident lifecycles from emergency phone reporting through forensic evidence collection and final court submission. Computer operators stationed at district control centers must process voluminous textual transmissions including daily case diaries, special surveillance bulletins, and statutory notices under stringent time constraints.\n\nTypographical precision remains foundational to digital governance within law enforcement agencies. Any transcription oversight or inadvertent omission during records entry can compromise the legal validity of prosecutorial documentation or cause administrative delays during judicial hearings. Candidates preparing for state recruitment examinations are therefore evaluated not merely on gross finger velocity across the keyboard, but fundamentally on sustained concentration, typographical discipline, and the ability to maintain above eighty-five percent accuracy throughout the full fifteen-minute testing interval. Consistent keyboard drills and systematic text auditing cultivate the motor memory necessary for high-speed administrative documentation."
