    id: "ar-7515",
    testNumber: 124,
    title: "Test #124: India Reverts to 2020 LAC Patrolling Terms",
    language: "english",
    category: "up_police_asi",
    duration: 15,
    wordCount: 628,
    difficulty: "medium",
    date: "2024-10-24",
    text: "After long negotiations, India and China have finally agreed to return to the patrolling arrangements along the LAC in eastern Ladakh that were in place before the Galwan clashes in 2020. The agreement covers the areas of Depsang and Demchok. External affairs minister S Jaishankar had recently said that about 75% of disengagement problems with China had been sorted out and that the key issue was the increasing militarisation of the frontier. Now, those negotiations are going on. We made some progress. We still have some things to do, he had said. Following the foreign ministry announcement, EAM Jaishankar said the two countries had gone back to where the situation was in 2020. We can say that the disengagement process with China has been completed. There are areas which for various reasons after 2020 because they had blocked us so we had blocked them. So what has happened is we have reached an understanding, which will allow the patrolling, he said. There was no specific mention of the withdrawal of tens of thousands of additional troops stationed by the two countries along the border in Ladakh and there was neither any statement from Beijing on the matter. Demchok is close to the southernmost part of the LAC in Ladakh, near the state border with Himachal Pradesh. A village in the region was the site of a Chinese incursion during the 1962 conflict but PLA troops did not venture beyond. It was the first place where China prevented Indian authorities from building civic infrastructure, including a road. Depsang Plains is a flat area near Daulat Beg Oldie in the northwest portion of the disputed Aksai Chin region in UT Ladakh. The disputed area had been occupied by China until India began making headway into the region and now has a road leading to it. Because of the flat terrain, it allows for easy movement of troops and vehicles, including tanks. Foreign secretary Vikram Misri said on Monday the agreement was thrashed out by Indian and Chinese negotiators after weeks of talks aimed at resolving the issues that arose after the Chinese military action in eastern Ladakh in 2020. Indian and Chinese troops first clashed on May 5, 2020, on the north bank of the Pangong Tso lake. There was a major clash on the night of June 15 between an Indian patrol and PLA troops in Galwan Valley with casualties on both sides. Amid claims and counter-claims regarding the capture of Indian territory in May and June 2020, there were satellite images showing China constructing bunkers and trenches and setting up tents along Pangong Tso lake. It even reportedly built a pier on the lake for boats. After the 2020 clashes, China aggressively built up its presence along the LAC in Ladakh, including by bringing in troops and armoured vehicles.\n\nIn the operational architecture of Uttar Pradesh Police, technological adaptation has transformed administrative transparency and tactical responsiveness. The integration of modern analytical dashboards enables precinct supervisors to track incident lifecycles from emergency phone reporting through forensic evidence collection and final court submission. Computer operators stationed at district control centers must process voluminous textual transmissions including daily case diaries, special surveillance bulletins, and statutory notices under stringent time constraints.\n\nTypographical precision remains foundational to digital governance within law enforcement agencies. Any transcription oversight or inadvertent omission during records entry can compromise the legal validity of prosecutorial documentation or cause administrative delays during judicial hearings. Candidates preparing for state recruitment examinations are therefore evaluated not merely on gross finger velocity across the keyboard, but fundamentally on sustained concentration, typographical discipline, and the ability to maintain above eighty-five percent accuracy throughout the full fifteen-minute testing interval. Consistent keyboard drills and systematic text auditing cultivate the motor memory necessary for high-speed administrative documentation."
